amulet.descripcion:
Amulets are items carried for good luck and protection. Your amulet might be a magical diagram, a religious symbol, a preserved body part such as a rabbit's foot, or a lucky coin. Amulet implements are associated with the harrow suit of shields and the astrological signs of the bridge and the ogre.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.ALcWRnRjvuPKu4nV inline]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.l3X6D8uMlt2y6vGS inline]
Intensify Vulnerability
Your amulet repels the creature's attempts to harm you. You gain a +2 status bonus to AC and saves against the target of your Exploit Vulnerability.
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.l3X6D8uMlt2y6vGS inline]

bell.descripcion:
Bells symbolize the power that sounds and emotions hold over others, soothing with one tone and startling with another. Bells, drums, finger cymbals, and other percussion instruments are most typical, but these implements can be any type of portable musical instrument that is played with one hand. Bell implements are associated with the astrological signs of the daughter and the blossom.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.M0UnQTqofeg1npcl inline]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.4xDghsFgGldaNj9Y inline]
Intensify Vulnerability
Your reinforced bell can reach into the most basal part of the target's mind, priming it to be vulnerable to the bell's effects. When you successfully Strike the target of your Exploit Vulnerability, your bell implement plays a haunting tone and the creature takes a -2 status penalty on saves against your Ring Bell for 1 round, or a -3 status penalty on a critical hit. This effect has the auditory trait.
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Mu6lZ0H7hmsgKDKH inline]

censer.descripcion:
Censer implements are vessels in which incense is burned, producing a haze of smoke that often carries a potent odor. Censers, thuribles, and other similar items are routinely used in religious ceremonies and represent practices that alter the atmosphere of a place, usually to drive off unwanted forces. Censer implements are often associated with the harrow suit of stars and the astrological sign of the underworld dragon.

Goblins, especially those of the Chitterwood, have created a kind of censer that is known as a stink torch. Despite its name, a stink torch doesn't give off any illumination when lit, just a haze of acrid smoke.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.5cpC7dZjEDuSAZef inline=true]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.ZOlDwzTQ9PDJsJSR inline=true]
Intensify Vulnerability
The incense within your censer is particularly dangerous to your targets. When you successfully Strike the target of your Exploit Vulnerability while it is within your smoke cloud, the creature takes 1d6 persistent damage (or 2d6 on a critical hit).
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.TR5AzAIDbTxbHrO9 inline=true]

chalice.descripcion:
Chalice implements are vessels that fill with liquid, associating them with healing, nourishment, and life. Your chalice might be a traditional cup or goblet, but it could also be a small amphora, a polished gourd, or even a hollowed-out skull. Chalice implements are associated with the astrological signs of the mother and the newlyweds, as well as the sea dragon.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.UfUqPcPcrGgRJCO3 inline]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.T6p6lZnGupq3CX6A inline]
Intensify Vulnerability
Your reinforced chalice can collect a creature's life force from a distance to become empowered. While you're within 30 feet of the target of your Exploit Vulnerability, you increase the effect if someone Drinks from the Chalice. Add additional temporary Hit Points equal to your level if the drinker sips, or add twice your level to the Hit Points regained if the drinker drains the chalice.
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.rW3xdQPTNptQIcL5 inline]

lantern.descripcion:
Lantern implements shine the light of revelation to part shadows and expose truth. You might use a common glass lantern, torch, paper lantern, or other similar light source. Lantern implements are associated with the harrow suit of stars and the astrological signs of the lantern bearer and the archer.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.tBI15UqeQH7PLzAK inline]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.QK5ojonup9AQBg4O inline]
Intensify Vulnerability
Your lantern's light flares and burns bright, leaving no shadows in which secrets and enemies can hide. The emanation of your lantern's aura doubles in size. Against the target of your Exploit Vulnerability, the status bonuses from the lantern's initiate benefit increase to +2. The creature takes a –2 status penalty to Deception checks and Stealth checks as long as it's within the aura. Additionally, the target of your Exploit Vulnerability can't be Concealed while it's in the lantern's aura, though it still can potentially become hidden or undetected using cover or means other than the concealed condition.
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.k9d3rDhYnHwLI8XF inline]

mirror.descripcion:
Mirror implements represent misdirection, illusion, and sleight of hand, bending and shifting a perspective and the way you look at things. While larger mirrors hold the same mystic connotations, thaumaturges always choose small, portable, handheld mirrors as implements so they can use them easily while adventuring. Mirror implements are associated with the harrow suit of keys, and the astrological signs of the stranger and the swallow.
Initiate Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.AehJwnLCUyASCQlu inline]
Adept Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.AEibGHmDzLiqGR0F inline]
Intensify Vulnerability
Reinforcing your mirror lets it play tricks on your enemy's senses as it bends light this way or that. You become Concealed to the target of your Exploit Vulnerability as your mirror warps its perceptions. As normal for concealment where your overall location is still obvious, you can't use this concealment to Hide or Sneak.
Paragon Benefit
@Embed[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.jyfTDSYuzXaNuJ2r inline]
